 "id": "gripper-palm-fdm",
 "brief": "The palm of my robot arm's gripper, ASA on FDM, printed bottom down (layers along +Z). Its bottom\nface (z = 0) screws to the wrist with four M3 screws coming up into heat-set inserts at (+/-20,\n+/-20): 4.2 mm holes 6 mm deep, 1.5 mm of wall round each, and a flat 7.5 mm landing round each\nwhere the wrist flange clamps. Two MG90S servos stand in it shafts up: bodies x = -11.5 to 11.5,\nz = 2 to 25, at y = 7 to 19.5 and y = -19.5 to -7, mounting ears (x = -16.5 to 16.5) resting at\nz = 18; they drop in from above, so keep clear over the bodies and ears. Each servo is fixed by\ntwo M2 self-tapping screws through its ears at (+/-14, +/-13.25) into 1.7 mm pilot holes 6 mm deep\nfrom z = 18 down, with 5 mm bosses and a flat 5.8 mm landing under each ear. A 25 g camera (body\nx, y = -6 to 6, z = 10 up) is glued on a 12 x 12 x 3 mm pad (z = 7 to 10); its cables drop through\nan 8 mm hole along Z at (0, 0). The palm fits in x = -30 to 30, y = -26 to 26, z = 0 to 22. Each\nfinger's reaction is a force at its tip, (0, +/-13.25, 60), carried by its servo: squeezing, 10 N\npushing each finger outward (+Y on the +Y servo, -Y on the other); a held 0.8 kg part at 2 g\npulling both along +Z (half each; the camera feels 2 g too); a 20 N knock along +X on both tips; a\ntable crash, 40 N down (-Z) on the +Y tip alone. Safety factor 3, under 20 g.",
